{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeaNdVZhAwDPqz7MhLxuQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L7UXAp593yjuwoDNLZBj9D","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/debug/debug-cluster/crictl/","prompt":"Output the page as raw markdown, copied word for word. This is a transcription task, NOT a summarization task. Do not write any sentence of your own. Do not add headings like \"Overview\" or \"What is crictl?\" that are not on the page. Do not write introductions such as \"Here's a comprehensive overview\".\n\nBegin your output with the page's own first sentence and transcribe straight through, preserving: every heading exactly as worded, every paragraph in full, every code block with its exact contents including sample command OUTPUT tables (POD ID / CREATED / STATE / NAME / NAMESPACE / ATTEMPT columns, CONTAINER / IMAGE / CREATED / STATE / NAME / ATTEMPT columns), every note and caution admonition, and the full \"Mapping from docker cli to crictl\" table if present.\n\nTranscribe these sections in order: the opening paragraphs defining crictl and CRI, \"Before you begin\", \"Installing crictl\", \"General usage\", \"Example crictl commands\" and all its subsections (List pods, List images, List containers, Execute a command in a running container, Get a container's logs, Create a container, Start a container, Run a pod sandbox), and any concluding sections.\n\nTranscribe verbatim any admonition warning that crictl is not the same as docker or that using crictl to create pods/containers on a running cluster can cause problems."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21610,"cache_read_input_tokens":73038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21610},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"dia