{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D9H1bL7BCRQZLWisQjsXyu","type":"tool_result","content":"Based on the provided documentation, here are the exact entries from the kube-apiserver options table:\n\n**1. `--event-ttl` row:**\n\"--event-ttl duration     Default: 1h0m0s\" with description: \"Amount of time to retain events.\"\n\n**2. `--default-not-ready-toleration-seconds` row:**\n\"--default-not-ready-toleration-seconds int     Default: 300\" with description: \"Indicates the tolerationSeconds of the toleration for notReady:NoExecute that is added by default to every pod that does not already have such a toleration.\"\n\n**3. `--default-unreachable-toleration-seconds` row:**\n\"--default-unreachable-toleration-seconds int     Default: 300\" with description: \"Indicates the tolerationSeconds of the toleration for unreachable:NoExecute that is added by default to every pod that does not already have such a toleration.\"\n\n**4. `--min-request-timeout` row:**\n\"--min-request-timeout int     Default: 1800\" with description: \"An optional field indicating the minimum number of seconds a handler must keep a request open before timing it out. Currently only honored by the watch request handler, which picks a randomized value above this number as the connection timeout, to spread out load.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4cae61e-42df-484d-af84-1dcbf8c0a281","uuid":"e68e741f-838e-4339-8775-2af494974e0f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:47:23.673Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":76527,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Based on the provided documentation, here are the exact entries from the kube-apiserver options table:\n\n**1. `--event-ttl` row:**\n\"--event-ttl duration     Default: 1h0m0s\" with description: \"Amount of time to retain events.\"\n\n**2. `--default-not-ready-toleration-seconds` row:**\n\"--default-not-ready-toleration-seconds int     Default: 300\" with description: \"Indicates the tolerationSeconds of the toleration for notReady:NoExecute that is added by default to every pod that does not already have such a toleration.\"\n\n**3. `--default-unreachable-toleration-seconds` row:**\n\"--default-unreachable-toleration-seconds int     Default: 300\" with description: \"Indicates the tolerationSeconds of the toleration for unreachable:NoExecute that is added by default to every pod that does not already have such a toleration.\"\n\n**4. `--min-request-timeout` row:**\n\"--min-request-timeout int     Default: 1800\" with description: \"An optional field indicating the minimum number of seconds a handler must keep a request open before timing it out. Currently only honored by the watch request handler, which picks a randomized value above this number as the connection timeout, to spread out load.\"","durationMs":4446,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/kube-apiserver.md"}}
