{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeaNon7ddghmZdwtxGX4G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PYLKWQMgP2STa2MuWfQXzX","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/quick-reference/","prompt":"Transcribe, word for word, ONLY the troubleshooting-relevant portions of this kubectl cheat sheet. Do not summarize or paraphrase; copy the command lines and their trailing comments exactly.\n\nReproduce in full these sections and every command line inside them:\n- \"Interacting with running Pods\" — every `kubectl logs` variant (including --previous / -p, -c, --all-containers, -f, --tail, --since, and logs with a label selector), `kubectl attach`, `kubectl exec`, `kubectl top pod`, `kubectl top node`, `kubectl port-forward`.\n- \"Interacting with Deployments and Services\" if it contains diagnostic commands.\n- \"Viewing, finding resources\" — specifically any line about sorting or listing Events (for example `kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp`, `kubectl events`, or listing warning events with `--types=Warning`), and any line showing `kubectl get pods -o wide`.\n- \"Describe commands with verbose output\" — every line.\n- \"Interacting with Nodes and cluster\" — every line, including `kubectl cluster-info`, `kubectl get nodes`, `kubectl describe node`, `kubectl cordon`, `kubectl drain`, `kubectl top node`.\n- Any \"Kubectl output verbosity and debugging\" verbosity table.\n\nPreserve the exact flag spellings and the exact comment text after each command."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14699,"cache_read_input_tokens":106367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14699},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent