{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01488RvmY3DUeT7NGPAmDdzg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Diagnostic-Relevant Sections from Kubernetes Nodes Documentation\n\n## Node status\n\nA Node's status contains the following information:\n\n*   [Addresses](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#addresses)\n*   [Conditions](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#condition)\n*   [Capacity and Allocatable](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#capacity)\n*   [Info](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#info)\n\nYou can use `kubectl` to view a Node's status and other details:\n\n    kubectl describe node <insert-node-name-here>\n    \n\nSee [Node Status](/docs/reference/node/node-status/) for more details.\n\n---\n\n## Node conditions\n\nNOT PRESENT - The complete conditions table and surrounding paragraphs are not included in the provided content. The page content is truncated with \"[Content truncated due to length...]\" before this section.\n\n---\n\n## Node heartbeats\n\nHeartbeats, sent by Kubernetes nodes, help your cluster determine the availability of each node, and to take action when failures are detected.\n\nNOT PRESENT - The complete section including both heartbeat forms, namespace details, update intervals, and numeric values are not included in the provided content. The page content ends with the truncation notice immediately after this heading.\n\n---\n\n## Node controller\n\nNOT PRESENT - This section is not included in the provided content due to truncation.\n\n---\n\n## Graceful node shutdown\n\nNOT PRESENT - This section is not included in the provided content.\n\n---\n\n## Non-graceful node shutdown handling\n\nNOT PRESENT - This section is not included in the provided content.\n\n---\n\n## Node capacity\n\nNOT PRESENT - This section is not included in the provided content.\n\n---\n\n## Node topology\n\nNOT PRESENT - This section is not included in the provided content."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4cae61e-42df-484d-af